@* Docker path warning: one component for every screen that takes a
   filesystem path. MelodyBridge runs inside Docker for most users, and
   the scanner only sees the paths as mounted INTO the container, so a
   host path typed here silently matches nothing. *@
<div class="mount-warning" role="note">
    <Icon Name="alert" Size="18" Class="mount-warning-icon" />
    <div>
        <strong>Docker users: type the path as the container sees it.</strong>
        The scanner reads paths from inside MelodyBridge. If the app runs
        in Docker, a host path (for example <code>C:\Music</code> or
        <code>/home/me/Music</code>) is invisible to it; use the container
        path your volume is mounted as (for example <code>/music</code>).
        Check the <code>volumes:</code> section of your compose file to see
        the mapping, and make sure the folder is actually mounted. Without
        a correct mount, the scanner finds zero files and downloads start
        from scratch.
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    // No parameters: the warning is always the same everywhere, which is
    // the point of having one shared component instead of per-page copies.
}
